# --- Credentials: none exist in this repo today. These rules are preventive. ---
# Drive access currently runs through the claude.ai MCP connector (server-side OAuth),
# so there is no local client_secret/token file. If a future pipeline ever uses a
# local Google API client, its secrets land here and MUST stay untracked.
*.env
.env*
client_secret*.json
credentials*.json
token*.json
service-account*.json
service_account*.json
*oauth*.json
.netrc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
*.keychain*

# --- Local tool/editor state ---
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db

# --- Incidental artifacts, not project sources ---
# A dump of a Claude Code terminal session. Scanned clean of secrets, but it is a
# conversation transcript rather than a build input -- excluded from a PUBLIC repo
# by default. Delete this line if you want it tracked.
full terminal convo.pdf

# --- Local caches / scratch (pipeline byproducts, not history) ---
.cache/
cache/
*.log
*.tmp
scratch/

# --- Build artifacts: pure functions of data/raw/ plus the scripts, which git
# already versions. Rebuild with `python3 scripts/build_dataset.py`.
# History is data/raw/ -- that is the part that cannot be regenerated (the
# rankings endpoint has no season pin, so a past season's official RPI table is
# gone once the season rolls over). Store raw, derive everything else.
data/data_2025.json
data/snapshots/
data/rpi_2025.json
data/bakeoff_2025.json

data/data_*.json
data/rating_*.json
data/bakeoff_*.json
data/rpi_2*.json

# ── BALLOT HISTORY IS PRIVATE ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cody's own weekly VolleyTalk ballots: his ranking, his private per-team
# notes, and his written reasons for overruling the model. This repository is
# PUBLIC, so a tracked ballot file would be world-readable the moment the
# daily job committed it.
#
# ⚠ EVERY SEASON, not just this one -- the glob is the point. An ignore rule
# naming 2026 protects nothing on 1 January.
#
# It stays DURABLE where it matters: scripts/ballot.py appends to this file on
# local disk and never rewrites it, so history survives here in full. What
# changes is only that git stops carrying it off this machine.
#
# ⚠ NOT gitignored as a way of hiding a leak: checked before writing this rule
# and no ballot file has ever been committed, at any path, on any ref.
data/ballots_*.jsonl

# Per-game player lines. For FINISHED seasons this is a resumable working file
# and only the aggregate is committed -- /boxscore is ID-addressed, so it can be
# re-crawled at will.
#
# THE LIVE SEASON IS DIFFERENT, and this is a correction paid for in a failed
# job. "Re-crawlable" turned out to carry an asterisk: a 2024 backfill ran fine
# for ~10k requests and then the API began hanging on every second one, leaving
# that season stuck at 43% and all of it August-September. Whatever that was,
# it means data you decline to take today may not be gettable later.
#
# The daily pipeline also runs on a FRESH CHECKOUT every morning. If this file
# is ignored, CI has nothing to resume from: it would refetch the whole season
# each day and throw the result away at the end of the job.
#
# So the live season's rows are committed. They arrive append-only at a few
# kilobytes a match, and they are what availability and next year's returning
# production are built from.
data/raw/2024/playerbox.jsonl
data/raw/2025/playerbox.jsonl

# Saved VolleyTalk pages (PDF / HTML / webarchive). Kept on disk, out of the
# PUBLIC repo on purpose: they contain forum members' posts, usernames and
# avatars, and committing them here would republish other people's writing.
# They are also redundant -- the anonymous live fetch is byte-identical to a
# logged-in save (measured, docs/data_sources.md §3), so nothing is preserved
# by keeping them under version control.
*Volley Talk*.pdf
*Volley Talk*.html
*Volley Talk*.webarchive

# Cody's personal quick-reference hub. Generated by scripts/build_cody_hub.py
# and read by nobody -- deleting it cannot affect a build. Kept out of this
# PUBLIC repo because Cody/data/tv_listings_2026.txt is transcribed from a
# VolleyTalk thread (same reasoning as the saved forum pages above).
Cody/

# The prediction log is the one file here that CANNOT be rebuilt: it records what
# the model said before each match was played, and re-deriving it afterwards from
# data that includes the outcome would be a fit, not a forecast. Committed.
!data/raw/2026/prediction_log.jsonl

# Raw play-by-play payloads: ~58 KB/game, ~296 MB/season, and we only need six
# names a game out of them. scripts/crawl_pbp.py extracts to lineups.jsonl and
# discards the raw by default; --keep-raw writes this file for local debugging.
# It must never be committed -- the daily workflow runs `git add data/raw`, so
# without this line CI would quietly push it to a PUBLIC repo.
data/raw/*/pbp.jsonl

# Reference PDFs saved from ncaa.com (official bracket, AVCA rankings). Read for
# facts, kept OUT of this PUBLIC repo: they are NCAA/AVCA publications and
# committing them republishes someone else's document. Same reasoning as the
# VolleyTalk saves above. The FACTS they contain (format, field size, seeding
# rules) are written up in docs/championship_format.md, which is ours.
*NCAA.com.pdf
*Official Bracket*.pdf
*AVCA Rankings*.pdf

# Research briefs returned by the other seats (Claude app / Gemini). They are
# other people's write-ups quoting beat reporters and terms-of-service text, and
# this repo is PUBLIC. Their FINDINGS are recorded in CLAUDE.md and docs/ in our
# own words; the documents themselves stay local.
NCAA D-I Women's Volleyball 2026_*.md
NCAA D-I Women's Volleyball 2026_*.pdf
2026 NCAA Division I Women's Volleyball_*.md
2026 NCAA Division I Women's Volleyball_*.pdf
NCAA D-I Women's Volleyball Stats Build_*.md
NCAA D-I Women's Volleyball Stats Build_*.pdf

# Local-only source documents: research returned by other seats, official
# NCAA/AVCA PDFs, VolleyTalk saves, superseded handoffs. None of it is ours to
# republish and the repo is PUBLIC. Findings live in CLAUDE.md and docs/.
reference/
.DS_Store

# Third-party play-by-play mirror (MIT, ncaavolleyballr). 739 MB per season
# and not ours to redistribute. Derived rotations ARE ours and are committed.
data/raw/*/pbp/

# Hand-drawn player art: likenesses of named college athletes, private page
# only. Never published.
Cody/
assets/digby_*_full.png

# Loose image/archive drops in the repo root. These arrive by AirDrop or export
# with UUID names and got committed on 2026-08-23 -- including a drawn likeness
# of a named college athlete, onto a PUBLIC repo. Ignore the shape, not the
# individual files, or the next one lands the same way.
/[0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F][0-9A-F]-*.PNG
/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]-*.png
/*.webarchive
/NCAA Women's Volleyball 2026.*
/Style Examples.pdf

# AVCA published workbooks (All-America, all-region, players of the week).
# Parsed into data/avca_awards.json, which IS committed; the source workbooks
# are AVCA's to distribute.
AVCA-*.xlsx

# EVERY PDF, not one pattern per drop. The targeted rules above (*NCAA.com.pdf,
# *Official Bracket*.pdf, ...) each had to be added after a file appeared, and a
# bare name like `2025.pdf` slips past all of them -- it did. These are
# NCAA/AVCA/forum publications whose own sheets say "no commercial use without
# written permission" and this repo is PUBLIC. Same call as the ncaavolleyballr
# CSVs and the AVCA workbooks: read locally, commit only what we derive.
*.pdf
